// A `for` step clause is an expression in the AST but a statement in a block,
// so it is wrapped in the same `expr` node the parser would have built for
// `step;` written on its own line. The emitter then needs no special case.
expr_stmt(int a) {
  int id = newleaf("expr", a, 0, "", "");
} return int id;
